% podman-manifest-inspect 1

## NAME
podman\-manifest\-inspect - Display a manifest list or image index

## SYNOPSIS
**podman manifest inspect** [*options*] *listnameorindexname*

## DESCRIPTION

Displays the manifest list or image index stored using the specified image name.

## RETURN VALUE

A formatted JSON representation of the manifest list or image index.

## OPTIONS

@@option authfile

#### **--format**, **-f**=*format*

Change the default output format.  This can be of a supported type like 'json'
or a Go template.
Valid placeholders for the Go template are listed below:

| **Placeholder**  | **Description**                                         |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| .Annotations ... | map[] of annotations on the manifest list               |
| .ArtifactType    | Artifact type of the manifest list, if set              |
| .Manifests       | List of manifest descriptors (use with range)           |
| .MediaType       | Media type of the manifest list or image index          |
| .SchemaVersion   | Schema version of the manifest list                     |
| .Subject ...     | Subject descriptor of the manifest list, if set         |

@@option tls-verify

## EXAMPLES

Inspect the manifest of mylist:v1.11.
```
$ podman manifest inspect mylist:v1.11
```

Inspect the manifest using a custom Go template to display the media type.
```
$ podman manifest inspect --format "{{.MediaType}}" mylist:v1.11
application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json
```

Inspect the manifest using a Go template to list target platforms and digests.
```
$ podman manifest inspect --format '{{range .Manifests}}{{.Platform.OS}}/{{.Platform.Architecture}} {{.Digest}}{{"\n"}}{{end}}' mylist:v1.11
linux/amd64 sha256:0f49f331d9212aff11b932863be4eb01cdf962969aa86dab7d1ee21ac6f5f52b
```

